<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Mutual Life sees bad debts down by 1999.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Mutual Life sees bad debts down by 1999.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo Mutual Life Insurance Co expects to reduce its bad loans to a manageable level by the end of the 1998/99 business year, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The official spoke at a news conference at which the company announced its business results for the first half of 1996/97 business year.</p>
